{
  "_help": [
    "Extra map layers. Each entry becomes a checkbox in the map's Layers menu, under its 'group'.",
    "files: file names or patterns in this data/ folder (* matches anything, so a new dated download",
    "  replaces the old one automatically; when several files match, the newest name wins).",
    "  Files must be GeoJSON in latitude/longitude (see the README for converting shapefiles or KML).",
    "fields: properties to keep, in popup order, as {property: label}. Everything else is dropped",
    "  so the map loads fast. values: optional lookups that turn codes into readable text.",
    "title: property shown in bold at the top of the popup.",
    "style: color (hex), radius (points, in pixels), fill (0-1, polygons), weight (outline width), border (outline color), shape (\"square\" draws points as small squares).",
    "categories: optional; color features by one property. Values not listed use 'other'.",
    "minZoom: hide the layer when zoomed out further than this (11 = citywide, 14 = neighborhood).",
    "on: true to show the layer when the map opens.",
    "where: optional filter, e.g. {\"field\": \"status\", \"equals\": \"Active\"} or \"not_equals\".",
    "style.icon: draw an icon instead of a dot (\"flask\"); style.size is its height in pixels.",
    "subtitle: property shown under the popup title. contacts: a property written like",
    "  'Lab Manager: Anna Weiss; Lab Tech: Reese LeVea', shown as one row per person.",
    "hover: true shows the popup title when the mouse is over a feature.",
    "where can also use \"in_list\" / \"not_in_list\" with the name of a list under \"lists\" at the bottom",
    "  of this file (the green infrastructure layers use this to sort asset types).",
    "file_labels: {file pattern: label}; the label is added to the popup subtitle, e.g.",
    "  'Vegetated Green Infrastructure · Regulated Project'.",
    "complete: features whose field starts with this text count as finished. group_field: a second",
    "  status field (DEP's status group); when the two disagree, a feature counts as finished only if",
    "  it has a valid construction date. only: \"complete\" keeps just finished features, \"pipeline\"",
    "  just unfinished ones (style.pipeline draws them hollow / hatched). built_date: date fields to",
    "  show (as month and year) for finished features; dates before min_year or in the future are",
    "  treated as errors and left out. Add \"_built\" to fields to show it, and \"_status\" for the",
    "  status (with the status group added when they disagree).",
    "categories classes can use \"list\" (a list under \"lists\") instead of \"values\"."
  ],
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "labs_active",
      "group": "Partner Laboratories",
      "name": "Active Labs",
      "files": [
        "CWQT_Partner_Labs*.geojson"
      ],
      "where": {
        "field": "status",
        "equals": "Active"
      },
      "title": "name",
      "subtitle": "status",
      "contacts": "lab_contacts",
      "style": {
        "icon": "flask",
        "color": "#0d4ab2",
        "size": 20
      },
      "on": true,
      "hover": true
    },
    {
      "id": "labs_historic",
      "group": "Partner Laboratories",
      "name": "Historic Labs",
      "files": [
        "CWQT_Partner_Labs*.geojson"
